hadiths[21]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22013","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq informed us, from Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of testimony is what its owner testifies before he is asked for it."
"22014","Ismail narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Hisham, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques, and let them go out unattractive."
"22015","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said ibn Hayyan, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Abi Amra, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that a man from Ashja among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died on the day of Khaybar, and that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Pray over your companion, so the faces of the people changed from that, and he said: Indeed your companion stole in the path of Allah, so we searched his baggage and found beads from the beads of the Jews not worth two dirhams."
"22016","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, Ata narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever provides breakfast for a fasting person will have, or will be written for him, the like of the reward of the fasting person, without decreasing from the reward of the fasting person anything, and whoever equips a warrior in the path of Allah will have, or will be written for him, the like of the reward of the warrior, in that nothing is decreased from the reward of the warrior."
"22017","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray in your houses and do not take them as graves."
"22018","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Labid, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Khallad ibn al-Saib, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me and said: O Muhammad, order your companions to raise their voices with the talbiya, for it is among the rites of Hajj."
"22019","Yazid narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salama, Salih ibn Kaysan and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salama narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile the rooster, for it calls to prayer, my father said, Abu al-Nadr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade reviling the rooster, and said: It announces the prayer."
"22020","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, that Abdullah ibn Qays informed him, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that he said: I will watch tonight the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I cushioned his threshold or his tent, then he prayed two light units, then he prayed two long units, then he prayed two units and they were shorter than the two before them, then he prayed two units shorter than the two before them, then he prayed two units shorter than the two before them, then he prayed two units shorter than the two before them, then he performed witr, so that is thirteen."
"22021","Abdullah said, and Musab narrated to us, Malik narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, that Abdullah ibn Qays ibn Makhrama informed him, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, then he mentioned the hadith, and Abd al-Rahman was not mentioned in the hadith of Malik from his father, and the correct is what Musab narrated from his father."
"22022","And likewise Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, Man narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, that Abdullah ibn Qays ibn Makhrama informed him, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, and the correct is what Musab and Man said from his father, and Abd al-Rahman did not mention in it from his father, and he erred in it."
"22023","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Abu Salama narrated to me, Busr ibn Said narrated to me, Ibn Khalid al-Juhani narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips a warrior has fought, and whoever leaves behind a warrior among his family with good has fought."
"22024","Ribi, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Hisham, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques, and let them go out unattractive."
"22025","Abu Nuh Qurad narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan, from Ibn Abi Amra al-Ansari, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best of witnesses, who brings his testimony before he is asked for it, or informs of his testimony before he is asked for it."
"22026","Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Abi Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would impose hardship upon my ummah I would have commanded them with the siwak at every prayer, he said: So Zayd would go to the mosque with his siwak upon his ear in the place of the pen of the scribe, no prayer was established but he used the siwak before he prayed."
"22027","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from a freed slave of Juhayna, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Khalid, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding plunder and snatching."
"22028","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to me, from Abi al-Nadr freed slave of Umar ibn Ubaydullah, from Busr ibn Said, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the lost item, so he said: Announce it for a year, then if its seeker comes give it to him, otherwise know its container and its tie, then use it, then if its seeker comes give it to him."
"22029","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ubayy ibn Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi narrated to me, Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan narrated to me, Kharija ibn Zayd ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amra al-Ansari narrated to me, Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani narrated to me, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best of witnesses is one who fulfills his testimony before he is asked for it."
"22030","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, Yaqub ibn Khalid informed me, from Abi Salih al-Samman, Yahya said, and I know only that he said, from Zayd ibn Khalid, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Quraysh, and the Ansar, and Aslam, and Ghifar, or Ghifar and Aslam, and whoever was of Ashja and Juhayna, or Juhayna and Ashja, are allies, my freed clients, they have no patron besides Allah and His Messenger."
"22031","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever touches his private part let him perform ablution."
"22032","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Umara ibn Abdullah ibn Tuma narrated to me, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sheep for sacrifices among his companions, and gave me a young kid goat from the goats, he said: So I came to him with it and said: O Messenger of Allah it is a kid, he said: Sacrifice it, so I sacrificed it."
"22033","Surayj narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning al-Darawardi, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays two prostrations without inattention in them, Allah forgives him what preceded of his sin."
